@@ -208,6 +214,17 @@ Since the underlying FIDO2/CredMan backends are accessed via the Java layer,
 but the browser UI and autofill systems are orchestrated in C++ Chrome layers,
 `WebauthnBrowserBridge` acts as the bidirectional JNI bridge.
 
+Credential Manager lifecycle events are routed separately through
+`WebauthnCredManBridge`. This common, stateless JNI bridge is available to both
+Chrome and WebView embedders. It does not expose Chrome's credential picker;
+WebView conditional requests are surfaced through the existing Android
+Autofill integration. Chrome enables per-frame CredMan delegates through its
+`WebAuthnClientAndroid`; the common CredMan bridge explicitly enables the same
+delegate factory for a `WebContents` when a conditional request becomes
+pending, without requiring WebView to install a Chrome UI client.
+The CredMan lifecycle methods are therefore not part of
+`WebAuthnClientAndroid` or `WebauthnBrowserBridge`.
+
